00:00:00,510 --> 00:00:01,840
C.

2
00:00:01,840 --> 00:00:11,730
Daniel and Amy are talking about what they can do to help protect forests, work in pairs and talk about the topic.

3
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:15,230
Use the conversation below as a model.

4
00:00:15,230 --> 00:00:20,880
What can we do to help protect forests, Daniel?

5
00:00:20,880 --> 00:00:25,595
Well, we should not throw rubbish in forests.

6
00:00:25,595 --> 00:00:29,740
We can also work with a clean-up group.

7
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:32,050
That's a good idea.

8
00:00:32,050 --> 00:00:39,260
Rubbish causes pollution and damages the forest ecosystem. That's true.

9
00:00:39,260 --> 00:00:44,020
And maybe we can take our own chopsticks when eating out.

10
00:00:44,020 --> 00:00:47,570
It's a great way to save trees.

11
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:53,360
Yes, we can encourage people to protect forests too.

12
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,690
You said it!

13
00:00:55,690 --> 00:01:00,780
We can show people different ways to save forests.

14
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:09,120
Yes, education and knowledge are useful tools to help keep forests safe. I agree.
